From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: premohq <48417750+premohq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 04:40:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS5-ECAM's Switch side: its loading screen and in-game menu,
 drawn over Eden's frames

PS5-ECAM's port/eden/ingame.h, compiled in from the checkout PS5ECAM_PORT names (headless/ecam.cmake,
with Dear ImGui): its loading screen in place of ProsperoEden's (vulkan_hud_draw.inc leaves its own out),
and its in-game menu on touchpad click + Options, as on PS5-ECAM's other sides. Both are recorded into
the window pass around its own drawing (ecam_bridge.h). While the menu is up, player 1's controller is
the menu's and every game controller is still; the game runs on behind it, as Cemu's does behind
PS5-ECAM's Wii U menu, since system.Pause() stays out of main.cpp (tools/check-gpu-producer-stop.py).
What the menu changes (upscaling filter, frame generation, speed limit, volume) applies at once; Quit to
the library leaves as touchpad + L1 does.
